      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camden%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1824 the village changed its name to Newcomb after State Senator George Newcomb.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camden%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1831 Camden was incorporated, marking its formal establishment as a village.",
